1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire
Knight of the Ribbon

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Knight of the Ribbon,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Twenty-Sixth Episode
The Icicle Queen
Snow Queen

15
00:02:19,590 --> 00:02:20,590
Copperland...

16
00:02:22,310 --> 00:02:25,200
Soon, every country in the world will be mine.

17
00:02:25,315 --> 00:02:27,119
Now, the next country to take is...

18
00:02:27,143 --> 00:02:28,826
Silverland.

19
00:02:30,170 --> 00:02:31,460
Oh, Freeze?

20
00:02:31,855 --> 00:02:33,720
Silverland is a beautiful country.

21
00:02:33,924 --> 00:02:35,900
I've always wanted it for myself.

22
00:02:36,415 --> 00:02:39,800
However, I hear that country has a formidable princess named Sapphire.

23
00:02:39,833 --> 00:02:41,393
Don't worry, Your Majesty.

24
00:02:41,584 --> 00:02:44,993
First, invite the girl to Coolland.

25
00:02:45,355 --> 00:02:46,653
Invite Sapphire?

26
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:48,366
And what then?

27
00:02:49,709 --> 00:02:51,926
While she's away, we'll have the King and Queen...

28
00:02:54,236 --> 00:02:56,200
tied up.

29
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:05,700
Conveniently enough, Silverland has wicked men like Duralumin and his cohort.

30
00:03:30,273 --> 00:03:32,480
Your Grace. Not a soul in sight.

31
00:03:33,234 --> 00:03:35,420
Ah, I'm sure it was right around here.

32
00:03:35,644 --> 00:03:38,240
Welcome, Lord Duralumin.

33
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,760
Well?

34
00:03:40,034 --> 00:03:42,326
Have you figured out a way to dispose of the

35
00:03:42,350 --> 00:03:44,600
King and Queen without anyone knowing?

36
00:03:45,170 --> 00:03:48,060
Is it true you'll step aside once that's done?

37
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:51,733
Her Majesty's word is absolute.

38
00:03:53,170 --> 00:03:56,093
All right, then leave the King and Queen to me.

39
00:03:56,239 --> 00:03:56,955
Are you sure about this?

40
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:59,595
You agreed so easily. We're using Mephisto, after all.

41
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:02,246
We're using Sapphire's boy's heart as bait.

42
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:03,773
I-I see.

43
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:16,013
I shall be on my way.

44
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:21,108
Are you sure she'll be alright on her own?

45
00:04:21,166 --> 00:04:22,079
Don't worry.

46
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:25,440
The one who summoned her is no ordinary person—it's Queen Icicle of Coolland.

47
00:04:26,166 --> 00:04:31,520
But rumors say she's a cold-hearted woman known as the Snow Queen.

48
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,813
Sapphire!

49
00:04:45,070 --> 00:04:46,285
Yo, Tink!

50
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:47,310
Where are you going?

51
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,453
To a northern country called Coolland.

52
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:54,000
Mmm, I wanna go too! — It's really cold, you know.

53
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:55,260
I don't care if it's cold!

54
00:04:55,485 --> 00:04:56,700
Take me with you!

55
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,940
All right then, let's go together.

56
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:01,340
Yay, I'm so happy! Come on, let's hurry!

57
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:02,960
Giddy-up!

58
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:18,400
How lucky that Tink is leaving on his own before we even have to make a move.

59
00:05:39,590 --> 00:05:41,965
- We're almost at the border. 
- It sure is vast.

60
00:05:42,730 --> 00:05:45,520
That queen must be really greedy.

61
00:05:47,065 --> 00:05:48,680
Don't talk bad about her, Tink.

62
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:04,780
Who's there?

63
00:06:05,035 --> 00:06:07,200
Did you come here knowing this is the border of Coolland?

64
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:08,960
What are you doing?

65
00:06:09,150 --> 00:06:11,020
I am Sapphire of Silverland!

66
00:06:12,045 --> 00:06:13,045
My apologies.

67
00:06:13,235 --> 00:06:15,160
The escort for Princess Sapphire has arrived.

68
00:06:15,475 --> 00:06:15,860
Go ahead.

69
00:06:20,975 --> 00:06:22,753
That's a convenient border.

70
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,660
Princess Sapphire, I've come to escort you.

71
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:39,667
Please get into the carriage.

72
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:42,407
No thanks, I have Opal.

73
00:06:42,431 --> 00:06:46,660
With all due respect, a cheap horse like that is unfit for a princess.

74
00:06:46,845 --> 00:06:48,313
You call this cheap?

75
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:53,640
Or are you saying you don't like the golden carriage sent by our Queen?

76
00:06:54,015 --> 00:06:55,015
The Queen?

77
00:06:56,310 --> 00:06:59,513
As a princess of Silverland, you must behave yourself.

78
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:04,193
Fine, fine! I'll get in!

79
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:07,800
Sorry, could you go back without me?

80
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:11,080
Tink, come on, get in.

81
00:07:11,780 --> 00:07:12,166
Okay.

82
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:13,920
Hold it!

83
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:15,720
What's wrong with that?

84
00:07:15,855 --> 00:07:17,220
Because I'm telling him to get on!

85
00:07:17,244 --> 00:07:19,120
My master is the Queen,

86
00:07:19,186 --> 00:07:19,946
not you.

87
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:22,600
Well, I'm that Queen's guest!

88
00:07:22,906 --> 00:07:23,553
There!

89
00:07:24,745 --> 00:07:25,940
Tink is my friend!

90
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,200
Should I get off?

91
00:07:27,605 --> 00:07:28,499
Don't pay any attention to him.

92
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,600
Let's go!

93
00:07:30,010 --> 00:07:31,180
Be my guest.

94
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:32,213
What?

95
00:07:32,730 --> 00:07:34,400
If you want to leave, go right ahead.

96
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:36,000
You see, it's a horseless carriage.

97
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,806
A horseless carriage?

98
00:07:39,070 --> 00:07:41,040
How to operate it is up to the rider.

99
00:07:41,585 --> 00:07:45,860
In our country, anyone but a complete bumpkin knows how to drive one.

100
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:48,180
Tink, do you know how?

101
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:49,646
Nope, not a clue.

102
00:07:52,110 --> 00:07:53,220
Let me give it a try anyway.

103
00:07:57,725 --> 00:07:59,060
Don't take it so lightly.

104
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,853
Wow, horseless carriages are amazing!

105
00:08:09,130 --> 00:08:10,966
It moves just by thinking about it!

106
00:08:11,165 --> 00:08:13,420
Don't just admire it—hurry up and stop it!

107
00:08:13,670 --> 00:08:16,293
But I don't know how to stop it!

108
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:19,240
So fast!

109
00:08:19,655 --> 00:08:22,536
Still, it all looks so desolate.

110
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:24,420
Yeah, it's the aftermath of war.

111
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:27,800
This is where this country fought Coolland.

112
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:30,100
The king must have died.

113
00:08:30,805 --> 00:08:32,059
I just feel that way.

114
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:35,793
Strange. Is no one living here?

115
00:08:39,399 --> 00:08:40,399
We're almost at the capital.

116
00:08:40,850 --> 00:08:43,159
You'll get to see the lively parts of Coolland.

117
00:09:05,179 --> 00:09:06,460
Wow, it's huge!

118
00:09:06,750 --> 00:09:08,796
Big houses everywhere you look.

119
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:10,440
Sapphire, don't get distracted!

120
00:09:10,575 --> 00:09:11,580
Forward, forward, forward!

121
00:09:11,805 --> 00:09:13,686
Oh no, it's locked!

122
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,640
All right, lower the bridge.

123
00:09:24,566 --> 00:09:25,800
How scary!

124
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,320
That is standard etiquette.

125
00:09:31,193 --> 00:09:32,833
Welcome, Princess Sapphire.

126
00:09:34,219 --> 00:09:35,941
That was pretty embarrassing, Sapphire.

127
00:09:42,969 --> 00:09:46,513
Presenting Her Majesty the Queen!

128
00:10:15,405 --> 00:10:17,719
I am Icicle, Queen of this land.

129
00:10:18,385 --> 00:10:19,733
Thank you for inviting me.

130
00:10:19,985 --> 00:10:21,400
I am Sapphire of Silverland.

131
00:10:21,780 --> 00:10:23,880
You're just as lively as they say.

132
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:27,660
I'm sorry for ruining your important meeting place.

133
00:10:27,885 --> 00:10:31,126
Don't worry, my kingdom has plenty of those.

134
00:10:31,245 --> 00:10:34,986
Um, Tink, where is my friend?

135
00:10:35,860 --> 00:10:39,380
Don't worry. He's waiting outside the castle.

136
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:43,335
No!

137
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:43,700
No!

138
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,973
Where are you taking me?!

139
00:10:57,999 --> 00:10:59,673
I said no! Let me go!

140
00:10:59,770 --> 00:11:01,063
Get in there!

141
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:10,380
What is this place?

142
00:11:10,759 --> 00:11:12,706
This is what you call a train.

143
00:11:12,966 --> 00:11:13,626
A train?

144
00:11:14,310 --> 00:11:17,380
That's right. An express bound for Hell.

145
00:11:17,725 --> 00:11:18,371
What?!

146
00:11:31,559 --> 00:11:34,013
Sapphire, help me!

147
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:37,460
What do you think of my kingdom, Lord Sapphire?

148
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:41,500
Don't you think it's the grandest in the world?

149
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:42,550
Yes, I do.

150
00:11:42,574 --> 00:11:47,240
See? Wouldn't you be happy to serve such a magnificent kingdom?

151
00:11:47,725 --> 00:11:51,953
Both Copperland and Ironland fought my kingdom and suffered terribly.

152
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:55,140
But I won't do that to your kingdom.

153
00:11:55,615 --> 00:11:56,800
What do you mean by that?

154
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:59,140
Figure that out yourself.

155
00:11:59,425 --> 00:12:01,060
You're clever enough to know.

156
00:12:01,785 --> 00:12:03,760
You saw what Coolland can do!

157
00:12:10,594 --> 00:12:13,506
Those hideous machines crushed Copperland!

158
00:12:22,630 --> 00:12:26,460
Those fireballs burned Ironland to the ground!

159
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:37,300
I see.

160
00:12:37,425 --> 00:12:39,640
You're telling us to submit before we get crushed, aren't you?

161
00:12:39,843 --> 00:12:44,160
Exactly. If you don't want to suffer a terrible fate, you'd better surrender quickly.

162
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:45,400
Well? What's your answer?

163
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:48,120
No!

164
00:12:48,565 --> 00:12:49,465
What?!

165
00:12:49,875 --> 00:12:50,880
Are you serious, Sapphire?!

166
00:12:51,715 --> 00:12:53,360
I absolutely refuse!

167
00:12:54,055 --> 00:12:56,300
Are you trying to destroy Silverland?

168
00:12:56,699 --> 00:12:59,486
Do you really want your beloved kingdom ruined?

169
00:12:59,825 --> 00:13:01,700
It's better than becoming your servant!

170
00:13:03,185 --> 00:13:08,180
I'll tell Father and the others that Coolland is a grand city, but a terrible one.

171
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:09,313
Goodbye!

172
00:13:09,885 --> 00:13:11,180
Well said, Sapphire.

173
00:13:11,530 --> 00:13:12,530
Remember this!

174
00:13:12,795 --> 00:13:15,760
You'll see what happens to anyone who insults Coolland.

175
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:16,780
Go!

176
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:18,380
To Silverland!

177
00:13:18,689 --> 00:13:20,860
Go and tell Duralumin...

178
00:13:20,980 --> 00:13:23,660
...that now is the time to summon Mephisto!

179
00:13:31,629 --> 00:13:34,526
Hey, isn't my friend waiting in this house?

180
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:37,293
Ah, he already headed back home.

181
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:39,640
He left?

182
00:13:39,739 --> 00:13:40,940
He probably couldn't wait any longer.

183
00:13:41,305 --> 00:13:43,020
Don't worry, if we hurry, we can easily catch up.

184
00:13:52,615 --> 00:13:54,320
That impudent Sapphire...

185
00:13:54,765 --> 00:13:57,240
Freeze, are the arrangements ready?

186
00:13:57,320 --> 00:14:03,280
Yes, yes, everything is taken care of. The messenger hawk should reach Duralumin any moment now.

187
00:14:31,739 --> 00:14:33,980
I've brought Mephisto with me.

188
00:14:34,070 --> 00:14:35,820
I heard Tink was away, so I flew right over!

189
00:14:36,045 --> 00:14:37,045
Are you sure about this?

190
00:14:37,465 --> 00:14:41,180
Of course. Now everything will go just as we planned.

191
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:44,120
You get Sapphire's boy's heart...

192
00:14:45,189 --> 00:14:47,280
...and you take over Silverland.

193
00:15:04,679 --> 00:15:06,500
I wonder how Sapphire is doing right now.

194
00:15:06,725 --> 00:15:07,580
Is she going to be okay?

195
00:15:07,665 --> 00:15:10,720
Don't worry. I'm sure she's fast asleep by now.

196
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:12,633
Zuborosha!

197
00:15:39,699 --> 00:15:41,620
What's with this whirlwind?

198
00:16:09,799 --> 00:16:11,200
Who are you?

199
00:16:11,986 --> 00:16:12,986
Cut it out!

200
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:14,720
You stand no chance against me!

201
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:16,620
Curse you!

202
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:18,340
Zuborosha!

203
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:24,279
What are you doing with that... Wait, what's this?

204
00:16:26,670 --> 00:16:27,670
I told you so!

205
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:29,680
Now stay quiet in there!

206
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,200
Be good!

207
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:34,640
Darling!

208
00:16:38,265 --> 00:16:39,265
S-Sapphire!

209
00:16:40,069 --> 00:16:41,100
Rest assured.

210
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:43,600
Soon, I'll bring Sapphire here too.

211
00:16:44,101 --> 00:16:46,206
Without her boy's heart, Sapphire won't...

212
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:47,780
Sapphire!

213
00:17:23,919 --> 00:17:25,246
What's wrong?

214
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:29,100
I'm terribly sorry. It broke down just as I was about to catch up.

215
00:17:29,594 --> 00:17:30,846
That's okay, I'll walk the rest of the way.

216
00:17:31,124 --> 00:17:32,306
I'm terribly sorry.

217
00:17:32,404 --> 00:17:34,340
The road to the border is that way.

218
00:17:41,179 --> 00:17:42,640
Hey, you can come out now.

219
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:45,913
Ah, that was rough.

220
00:17:46,269 --> 00:17:48,800
Even on Madame Freeze's orders, this isn't easy.

221
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,960
Let's hurry. We need to beat her there.

222
00:18:09,142 --> 00:18:10,169
Sapphire!

223
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,013
It's Tink!

224
00:18:12,099 --> 00:18:13,480
Help me!

225
00:18:13,534 --> 00:18:14,534
Wait!

226
00:18:14,559 --> 00:18:15,666
Give Tink back!

227
00:18:17,909 --> 00:18:19,753
What are you going to do with Tink?!

228
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:29,780
Tink!

229
00:18:39,179 --> 00:18:40,100
Tink, hold on...

230
00:18:40,124 --> 00:18:41,280
It's a dummy!

231
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:43,100
Damn it, we've been tricked!

232
00:18:45,190 --> 00:18:46,190
Somebody...

233
00:18:58,509 --> 00:18:59,800
Our defenses are holding up nicely.

234
00:19:01,609 --> 00:19:04,166
Now, let's march into Silverland. Ah!

235
00:19:15,689 --> 00:19:18,349
To die like this...

236
00:19:21,989 --> 00:19:23,433
My eyes... My eyes are open!

237
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:27,020
It hurts!

238
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:28,460
My eyes hurt!

239
00:19:30,399 --> 00:19:31,940
It's pitch black...

240
00:19:33,409 --> 00:19:35,444
I can't... I can't see anything...

241
00:19:35,468 --> 00:19:38,139
 I have to go back... to Silverland...

242
00:19:47,999 --> 00:19:49,520
Is anyone there?

243
00:19:50,214 --> 00:19:52,860
Is this the right way to Silverland?

244
00:20:21,109 --> 00:20:21,879
Where are you going?

245
00:20:22,109 --> 00:20:23,760
Do not cross the border to the left!

246
00:20:24,519 --> 00:20:26,260
The border... I remember!

247
00:20:26,599 --> 00:20:27,940
You're one of yesterday's guards!

248
00:20:28,225 --> 00:20:29,225
It's me, Sapphire!

249
00:20:29,309 --> 00:20:30,600
She's the princess of Silverland!

250
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:33,260
What did you say?

251
00:20:33,859 --> 00:20:36,806
As if we'd tolerate a filthy princess like that!

252
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:38,020
Oh, right!

253
00:20:38,264 --> 00:20:39,360
Like hell!

254
00:20:40,544 --> 00:20:41,544
What are you doing?!

255
00:20:42,924 --> 00:20:45,726
You're blind, yet you dare fight back?!

256
00:20:56,494 --> 00:20:57,874
Where are you?!

257
00:21:02,814 --> 00:21:04,920
Now, which way to Silverland?

258
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:06,440
Lead the way!

259
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:08,220
All right.

260
00:21:08,244 --> 00:21:09,293
I'll guide you.

261
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:12,960
Almost there.

262
00:21:13,304 --> 00:21:14,720
Even the smell of the wind has changed.

263
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:17,360
I'll get to see Mother soon!

264
00:21:32,125 --> 00:21:32,865
Thanks!

265
00:21:33,174 --> 00:21:35,220
I can manage on my own from here!

266
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:36,033
Goodbye!

267
00:21:37,834 --> 00:21:40,100
She's tough for a blind girl!

268
00:21:57,179 --> 00:21:58,340
Open the gate!

269
00:21:58,706 --> 00:21:59,200
It's me!

270
00:21:59,565 --> 00:22:00,565
It's Sapphire!

271
00:22:01,409 --> 00:22:02,649
Can't you hear me?

272
00:22:03,369 --> 00:22:05,226
I'm telling you, it's me!

273
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:09,500
"Sapphire"?

274
00:22:10,660 --> 00:22:11,660
Whose voice is that?

275
00:22:11,970 --> 00:22:12,970
Must be Duralumin's men, right?

276
00:22:13,365 --> 00:22:14,365
Why are you laughing?!

277
00:22:14,544 --> 00:22:15,544
What's so funny?!

278
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:19,293
What a lunatic!

279
00:22:19,419 --> 00:22:21,926
How dare you address the Grand Duke without his title!

280
00:22:22,959 --> 00:22:24,260
You're the gate guards!

281
00:22:24,460 --> 00:22:24,980
It's me!

282
00:22:25,224 --> 00:22:26,420
Don't you recognize Sapphire?

283
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:32,513
What are you guys talking about?!

284
00:22:32,624 --> 00:22:34,240
That's our line!

285
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:35,119
Enough out of you, lunatic!

286
00:22:35,199 --> 00:22:37,800
Prince Sapphire has already returned to the castle safe and sound!

287
00:22:37,801 --> 00:22:38,554
What?!

288
00:22:39,134 --> 00:22:40,959
That's impossible!

289
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:41,720
Listen!

290
00:22:41,934 --> 00:22:43,553
Let me see my father and mother!

291
00:22:43,949 --> 00:22:46,555
Then you'll see that I'm Sapphire!

292
00:22:46,579 --> 00:22:47,959
Sorry, but my father isn't here!

293
00:22:48,145 --> 00:22:49,145
My mother isn't here either!

294
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:50,740
What?!

295
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:54,606
They left the castle in my care and went on a secret journey!

296
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:56,020
You!

297
00:22:56,620 --> 00:22:57,160
That's right!

298
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:58,699
I'm the real Sapphire!

299
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:01,660
I recognize that voice!

300
00:23:02,060 --> 00:23:02,566
That's right!

301
00:23:02,859 --> 00:23:04,959
That's the guy who threw me off the cliff using Tink's voice!

302
00:23:06,699 --> 00:23:08,206
- Wait!
- Stop!

303
00:23:08,764 --> 00:23:10,313
So you're the one impersonating me?!

304
00:23:10,484 --> 00:23:11,913
Where did Mother go?!

305
00:23:12,529 --> 00:23:14,160
I don't need to answer you!

306
00:23:14,584 --> 00:23:16,140
I'll only tell you it's a distant island!

307
00:23:17,114 --> 00:23:18,506
Drive that lunatic away!

308
00:23:19,320 --> 00:23:20,320
Give them back!

309
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:25,001
Mother! Father! Give them back! Give them back!

310
00:23:30,729 --> 00:23:32,280
Open up!

311
00:23:34,829 --> 00:23:38,859
A fake Sapphire... The Snow Queen sure hatched a cruel scheme!

312
00:24:09,969 --> 00:24:10,969
<i>I won't give in!</i>

313
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,680
<i>I will not lose!</i>

314
00:24:13,340 --> 00:24:16,140
<i>Someday, I'm going to overturn this entire scheme!</i>

315
